---
import Img from "../../components/Img.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout path="/world/" title="The world" section="world" description="Mossy forests, lantern-lit towns and old stone ruins: the setting and mood of Lorehallow, early and subject to change.">
<section class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap page-head-art">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Early, and subject to change</p>
      <h1>The world</h1>
      <p class="lede">A warm, lantern-lit corner of a storybook fantasy: mossy forests, a timber town and old stone ruins on the hills. None of it is playable yet, and all of it may change.</p>
    </div>
    <Img src="icons/section_icons.png#world" alt="decorative" k={4} />
  </div>
</section>
<div class="wrap content">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="mood">The mood</h2>
    <p>Lorehallow is the hour after sunset. Cottage windows glow, someone has lit the lanterns along the road, and fireflies are coming out at the edge of the woods. It's a cosy place first and a dangerous one second: the danger is out past the last lantern, in the deep forest and the ruins nobody remembers building.</p>
    <p>The world starts small on purpose: one town and the land around it, handcrafted so every path leads somewhere. It grows only once that first place feels alive with people in it.</p>
    <h2 id="places">Places</h2>
    <ul class="stack-list">
      <li><strong>The town.</strong> Timber cottages with red roofs, a well, a market stall, an inn. Where players meet, trade and set out from.</li>
      <li><strong>The mossy woods.</strong> Old oaks, ferns and mossy rocks. Wolves and worse, and paths that are easy to lose.</li>
      <li><strong>The ruins.</strong> Broken arches and standing stones on the hills, older than the town and the start of most quests.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="notice">Names, places and the map are all still being worked out. Follow the <a href="/devlog/">devlog</a> to see them take shape.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="gallery">
    <figure>
      <div class="framed"><Img src="web/hero_scene.png" alt="The village at dusk: four adventurers on a dirt path between timber cottages, a great oak, a stone well and a market stall." max={960} /></div>
      <figcaption>The village at dusk, the landing page's key art. The painted scene came from an image generator; the four adventurers are hand-drawn.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <div class="framed"><Img src="style/reference.png" alt="A small scene built from hand-drawn tiles: grass and flagstones, an oak, a mossy rock, a lantern post, the corner of a cottage and the hero." max={960} /></div>
      <figcaption>The style reference: every new piece of art is checked against this little scene, built entirely from hand-drawn tiles and sprites.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <div class="framed"><Img src="web/og_card.png" alt="A traveller with a lantern on a winding path through dark hills toward a lit village and a mossy stone arch." max={960} /></div>
      <figcaption>The road in. A traveller with a lantern on the path to town.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <div class="framed"><Img src="web/not_found.png" alt="The hero standing lost on a forest path beside a signpost, with a question mark over their head." max={640} /></div>
      <figcaption>The woods, where it's easy to lose the path.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</div>
</Layout>
